Name: Unicode Common Locale Data Repository
Short Name: cldr
URL: https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr
     https://packages.debian.org/sid/unicode-cldr-core
Version: 44-0.1
Update Mechanism: Static (https://crbug.com/584852234)
License: Unicode-DFS-2016
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: yes

Description:
TheUnicode CLDR provides data files to support internationalisation.
Currently,this is used to provide emoji keywords and names to facilitate
searchin the Chrome OS emoji picker.

LocalModifications:
Onlythe files relevant to the following areas are currently checked out:
 - Emoji keywords for the following locals:
   - English (EN-US and en001 which is non-US English)
   - German
   - Japanese
   - Spanish
   - Swedish
   - Norwegian
   - Finnish
   - Danish
 - Rules for pluralization

The files come from the Debian package unicode-cldr-core, which installs
the CLDR release data.

To update, update the upstream version and artifact in crowbar.txtpb, then run
from this directory:
crowbar build --no-dry-run ./
copy.bara.sky lists every file it imports. If Chromium needs another CLDR
file, add it there.
